From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 577/577] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: show caps lock on the
 inside LED

The owner's choice, and what Gemian does. The red half of the inside LED
already followed kbd-capslock from userspace on the device. It takes effect
when leds-aw9120 loads; the other LEDs stay without a default trigger.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-a72.dts     | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-a72.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-a72.dts
index c881612b9..d54a0ac1c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-a72.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station-a72.dts
@@ -189,8 +189,9 @@ camera_front_ep: endpoint {
  * The AW9120 indicator LEDs: the five-LED block on the cover, the LED at its
  * end, and the red and blue pair inside. Groups and colours follow the Gemian
  * daemon; the enumerators follow the daemon's block numbers. The lowest current
- * on every output, as in Gemian outside its torch. Nothing is lit, and no LED
- * follows a trigger, until leds-aw9120 loads and userspace asks.
+ * on every output, as in Gemian outside its torch. Nothing is lit until
+ * leds-aw9120 loads. Caps lock then shows on the inside red; the rest wait for
+ * userspace.
  */
 &pio {
 	aw9120_pins: aw9120-pins {
@@ -372,6 +373,7 @@ led@12 {
 			function = LED_FUNCTION_INDICATOR;
 			function-enumerator = <7>;
 			led-max-microamp = <3500>;
+			linux,default-trigger = "kbd-capslock";
 		};
 
 		led@13 {
-- 
